    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That \"screaming\" or \"howling\" quality often comes from the sheer *pressure differential* and the turbulence created as the air is rapidly compressed and forced through the narrow passages of the turbo system. When the turbine spins up very quickly, the flow isn't perfectly laminar; instead, the air creates chaotic vortices around the blades. These intense, turbulent eddies are what translate into a much more aggressive, high-pitched sound than simple airflow. It's the sound of extreme energy conversion happening in a small space.",
      "source": "target",
